  "tour": "2026 Summer Tour",
  "notes": "<p>This show was Phish's 92nd performance at Madison Square Garden, featured a setlist comprised entirely of songs from the 1992 era of the band, included the return of long dormant antics from that time (trampolines in Mike's Song and bicycle kicks during I Am Hydrogen), and featured Trey wearing a sleeveless shirt (a common occurrence in 1992). This show also featured multiple bustouts: Glide (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-august-31-2021-shoreline-amphitheatre-mountain-view-ca-usa.html\">August 31, 2021</a>, or 225 shows), Cold as Ice (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-may-18-1992-the-flynn-theatre-burlington-vt-usa.html\">May 18, 1992</a>, or 1,468 shows), Love You (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-july-16-2016-gorge-amphitheatre-george-wa-usa.html\">July 16, 2016</a>, or 382 shows), Hold Your Head Up (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-july-29-2023-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa.html\">July 29, 2023</a>, or 135 shows), and The Vibration of Life (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-november-19-1996-municipal-auditorium-kansas-city-mo-usa.html\">November 19, 1996</a>, or 1,027 shows). Hold Your Head Up featured Fish on vacuum and a \"GOOAAAALLL\" announcement from Trey. Reba did not contain the whistling ending. My Friend, My Friend did not include the \"Myfe\"ending and contained The Well teases. Page teased the theme from <i>Speed Racer</i> in The Lizards. Harry Hood was aborted and quickly restarted.</p>",
  "permalink": "https://phish.net/setlists/phish-july-22-2026-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa.html",
